    "legend": "Different structural forms of chromosome&nbsp;21 gain resulting in Down syndrome by G-banded karyotype and corresponding chromosomal microarray result. <strong>A</strong>&nbsp;Three independent copies of chromosome&nbsp;21. <strong>B</strong>&nbsp;Unbalanced Robertsonian translocation between chromosomes&nbsp;14 and&nbsp;21. <strong>C</strong>&nbsp;Unbalanced translocation between two copies of chromosome&nbsp;21. <strong>D</strong>&nbsp;Chromosomal microarray data plot showing non-mosaic gain of all probes on the q-arm of chromosome&nbsp;21 (note there are no probes on the p-arm owing to an absence of unique DNA targets in that region); all Down syndrome cases show a similar chromosomal microarray result as this assay is not able to differentiate between the structural forms, which is important information for parental recurrence risk assessment. Red bars indicate the location of the additional copy of the chromosome&nbsp;21 q-arm.",
